supersonic (0.82.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. Failures in the client are reported in every build,
    not only a development one: a call into the engine that throws rejects,
    and a lost audio worklet warns; the clock's drift is logged when it moves
    rather than every second.

 -- Sam Aaron <sam@sonic-pi.net>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:03:34 +0100

supersonic (0.81.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. The engine logs through one channel on every
    platform, held through boot so nothing is lost; a subsystem the platform
    refuses (no Web MIDI backend) no longer fails the boot; synthdefs are
    handed to the engine one per block, paced by its replies; release
    binaries are stripped, with debug info split out.

 -- Sam Aaron <sam@sonic-pi.net>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:58:00 +0000

supersonic (0.80.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: scsynth on clockwork. The engine, device layer,
    transports, clock and Link now come from the clockwork submodule,
    archived into the orig tarball under clockwork/.

 -- Sam Aaron <sam@sonic-pi.net>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0000

